  "slug": "dark-energy-543b",
  "summary": "DESI-based fits and non-parametric reconstructions test evolving dark energy, with a reported phantom-divide crossing near z≈0.5–0.7.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is confronting departures from a cosmological constant with DESI BAO or full-shape data combined with CMB, supernovae and lensing. Within VCDM, three one-parameter vacuum histories are compared, with F42 favored by AIC when supernovae are included. A full-shape DESI DR1 power-spectrum analysis of the scalar-field-driven Fading Dark Sector model reports it outperforms CPL w0–wa. Two non-parametric reconstructions jointly infer the effective dark-energy density and gravitational response from CMB, DESI BAO, SNe and DES/LSS data. One reports a phantom-divide crossing near z≈0.5–0.7, and the other asks whether dark energy also clusters. A generalised axion-like quintessence model is tested against CMB, BAO, SNe, SH0ES, chronometer and GRB data. Peripheral work includes persistent-homology discrimination of cosmologies from z≈10 21-cm maps. It also includes a time-delay cosmography forecast in which mass-sheet-transform uncertainties reduce the decreasing-H0 trend to ~1σ.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
}
